To ensure the implementation aligns with the documented rule for `conformance.kernel.recovery`, specifically that the last object inside a code fence is prioritized as the scored object, regardless of parsing validity or fallback behavior. This includes clarifying whether the rule intends strict positional priority (last fenced object always wins) or parsing-dependent priority (last valid object wins), and adjusting either the rule or the code to eliminate ambiguity in cases where fenced objects are invalid or top-level objects appear after fences.